\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S11}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Continuous disparity error across estimation methods using the alternative tip+nodes fossil sampling scheme}. Relative disparity error returned from pre-ordination point ASE (ancestral state estimation), pre-ordination distribution ASE, post-ordination point ASE, post-ordination distribution ASE and no ASE. These disparity errors were calculated across three transition rates (fast (0.9), medium (0.1) and slow (0.01)), five simulated fossil sampling densities (100\%, 50\%, 15\%, 5\% and 0\%) and three disparity metrics (Sum of variances, sum of quantiles and mean pairwise distance). Values closest to 0 (dotted horizontal line) were most accurate; negative errors are under-estimates and positive are over-estimates.}}{9}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:Continuous nodes tips boxplot}{{S11}{9}{\textbf {Continuous disparity error across estimation methods using the alternative tip+nodes fossil sampling scheme}. Relative disparity error returned from pre-ordination point ASE (ancestral state estimation), pre-ordination distribution ASE, post-ordination point ASE, post-ordination distribution ASE and no ASE. These disparity errors were calculated across three transition rates (fast (0.9), medium (0.1) and slow (0.01)), five simulated fossil sampling densities (100\%, 50\%, 15\%, 5\% and 0\%) and three disparity metrics (Sum of variances, sum of quantiles and mean pairwise distance). Values closest to 0 (dotted horizontal line) were most accurate; negative errors are under-estimates and positive are over-estimates}{figure.caption.11}{}}
